# Battle System Architecture

## Core Development Principle
CRITICAL: Always implement changes with minimal scope and maximum focus. When fixing bugs or adding features:
- Only modify what is absolutely necessary to achieve the current goal
- Avoid scope creep and unnecessary "improvements"
- Stay focused on the immediate task
- Do not get sidetracked by unrelated issues unless specifically requested
- Keep logging minimal and focused on current development goal - never verbose unless absolutely necessary

## Core Principles
- Focus on proximity-based targeting and combat
- Maintain fluid, dynamic battalion movement
- Ensure simultaneous damage processing
- Support multi-battalion engagement

## Battle Flow

### 1. Pre-Battle Phase (3 seconds)
- Display countdown overlay
- Show deployment zones
- Animate network nodes and connection lines
- Initialize battalion health and positions

### 2. Active Battle Phase (20 seconds)
- Display battle timer at screen top
- Show battalion stats (health/quantity)
- Maintain animated network visualization
- Continue until victory conditions met or timer expires

### 3. Combat Mechanics

#### Battalion Movement
- Stop when any valid target (node/battalion) is in range
- Maintain position while target remains in range
- Follow moving targets until back in range
- Allow stacking of friendly battalions
- Movement not restricted to initial network lines

#### Targeting System
Core Rules:
- Always target nearest available enemy or node
- No maximum limit on battalions per target
- All battalion types follow same targeting rules
- Retarget only when:
  1. Current target destroyed/captured
  2. A closer target becomes available
  3. Current target moves out of range

#### Combat Processing
- Damage Application:
  - Process damage simultaneously when battalions are in range
  - No damage modifiers for multiple attackers
  - Continue until target health reaches 0
  - Prevent damage processing after health depleted

- Target Elimination:
  - Battalions: Remove when health reaches 0
  - Nodes: Change control state when capture threshold met
  - Immediately stop damage processing on eliminated targets

#### Node Control
- Node Health: 75% of total battalion health combined
- Control States:
  - Enemy (Red)
  - Neutral (Purple)
  - User (Blue)
- Capture occurs when damage threshold met
- Multiple battalions can attack same node

### 4. Victory Conditions
Battle ends when either:
- All enemy battalions destroyed AND all nodes captured
- 20-second timer expires
- Winner determined by:
  1. Complete elimination/capture
  2. Most nodes controlled at timer end
  3. Most surviving battalions at timer end

## Technical Requirements
- Efficient proximity-based target detection
- Smooth target following mechanics
- Simultaneous damage processing
- Immediate target state updates
- Support for multi-battalion stacking
- Accurate battle timer management